# Private-baseline commitment for V15X-TO-V1511-NO-LOSS-20260920

Recorded before any OpenRouter inference for this retention packet.

## Baseline assessment

Current evidence supports a strong but not final retention claim.

Expected preserved load-bearing 15.x domains include:
- foundational typed semantic graph / Design Forms / GSL lineage;
- Universal Per-Step Control Loop;
- rights, consent, privacy, Human-Effect Closure and authority separation;
- epistemic/provenance/uncertainty and causal closure machinery;
- physical safety / independent interlock / emergency constraints;
- justice, reputation and protected-reporting obligations;
- recursive/self-improvement qualification and protected-change boundaries;
- GCL and algebra/formal operator families;
- multi-agent independence and no-consensus-as-truth;
- transition, rollback/recovery and authority-migration semantics;
- specification != proof != implementation != validation != certification.

Known reasons NOT to declare no-loss yet:
1. compact v15.11 review projections are not themselves the full retained corpus;
2. PR #271 materialization is incomplete at audited head and public-release integrity is failing;
3. an earlier stale full-Catalogue binding was found and repaired in PR #273;
4. external adversarial retention review has not yet returned findings;
5. semantic equivalence is stronger than literal inventory/hash coverage and remains to be challenged.

## Falsification target

A successful challenger finding is any useful 15.x semantic obligation that is:
- absent from current v15.11 controlling source,
- weakened so its prior protection/meaning no longer follows,
- retained only as history when current behavior still depends on it,
- mapped to an owner that does not actually preserve its semantics,
- or represented by an identity/hash without recoverable current meaning.

Agreement is not the goal. One concrete counterexample is enough to defeat a blanket no-loss claim.

Status: BASELINE_COMMITTED / NO_EXTERNAL_MODEL_OUTPUT_SEEN.
